  "redTestChanges": [
    {
      "path": "scripts/check-pipeline-slim.test.mjs",
      "reason": "The spec was wrong: the AC-9 test destructured `{ code }` from `spawnSync()`, but spawnSync returns `{ status }` not `{ code }`. The `code` variable was permanently `undefined`, making the test impossible to pass regardless of implementation. Fixed by changing destructuring to `{ status: code, stdout, stderr }`. This is a RED-BROKEN correction, not a behavioral change to any assertion."
    },
    {
      "path": "scripts/check-pipeline-slim.test.mjs",
      "reason": "Re-invocation C-1 fix (type-annotation-only): added a JSDoc-typed `pair(key, value)` helper and replaced all `[c, makeXxx(c)]` / `[n, makeYxx(n)]` / inline-literal array pairs inside `new Map([...])` constructs with `pair(...)` calls. TypeScript checkJs cannot infer spread `.map()` returns as `[string, string]` tuples in array spreads, producing TS2769 errors at all 16 affected `new Map([...])` sites. No assertion logic changed."
    }
  ],
